\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces What this survey sampled in frequency. Each searched window is a horizontal segment on its host system's row, rows ordered by distance, coloured by nominal EIRP$_{5\sigma }$, with line weight distinguishing the drift-resolved (Class\nobreakspace  {}A) from the unresolved-spectral-excess (Class\nobreakspace  {}B) channelisation; the upper panel counts systems per gigahertz of sky frequency. The coverage is narrow, clustered and repeatedly revisited: 33{} islands concentrated near 230 and 345\,GHz, with summed window bandwidth $7.7\times $ the union, which is what the in-band transmitter fractions of Appendix\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:population} condition on (Scope of the constraints, \S  \ref  {sec:method}). Thresholds are nominal in the sense of \S  \ref  {sec:method}.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:waterfall}{{2}{4}{What this survey sampled in frequency. Each searched window is a horizontal segment on its host system's row, rows ordered by distance, coloured by nominal EIRP$_{5\sigma }$, with line weight distinguishing the drift-resolved (Class~A) from the unresolved-spectral-excess (Class~B) channelisation; the upper panel counts systems per gigahertz of sky frequency. The coverage is narrow, clustered and repeatedly revisited: \UnionIntervals {} islands concentrated near 230 and 345\,GHz, with summed window bandwidth $\GrossOverUnion \times $ the union, which is what the in-band transmitter fractions of Appendix~\ref {app:population} condition on (Scope of the constraints, \S \ref {sec:method}). Thresholds are nominal in the sense of \S \ref {sec:method}}{figure.2}{}}
