\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The dwell campaign. \emph  {(a)} Recovery of high per-integration-S/N injected carriers as a function of dwell fraction, pooling injected amplitudes $\geq 4\sigma $ per integration, from 3\,888{} trials over 12{} real windows. Recovery rises with dwell: a continuously transmitting carrier is the easiest case. This experiment establishes the dependence on temporal occupancy, not the absolute completeness at the survey detection threshold (that is the end-to-end campaign of Fig.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:completeness}).}}{10}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
