\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Selection function of the searched sample against a volume-limited reference census. Reference census: Gaia\nobreakspace  {}DR3 sources with $\varpi >0$, $\sigma _\varpi /\varpi \le 0.1$ and $1/\varpi \le 40$\,pc (17566 objects; 8594, 49 per cent, carry a \texttt  {teff\_gspphot} estimate). Sample: the 88 stars with at least one searched window, at the distances the search itself used. Temperatures are available for 52 of the 88 stars (all 88 matched to the 168-entry ALMA-covered census, 58 by exact name; 52 of those matches carry a temperature), so the temperature panel is normalised within each column over classified objects only, with $T_{\rm  eff}$ a proxy for spectral class. ``Ratio'' is the sample column fraction over the census column fraction: 1 means the sample tracks the reference population, $>1$ over-representation.}}{24}{table.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:selfunc}{{10}{24}{Selection function of the searched sample against a volume-limited reference census. Reference census: Gaia~DR3 sources with $\varpi >0$, $\sigma _\varpi /\varpi \le 0.1$ and $1/\varpi \le 40$\,pc (17566 objects; 8594, 49 per cent, carry a \texttt {teff\_gspphot} estimate). Sample: the 88 stars with at least one searched window, at the distances the search itself used. Temperatures are available for 52 of the 88 stars (all 88 matched to the 168-entry ALMA-covered census, 58 by exact name; 52 of those matches carry a temperature), so the temperature panel is normalised within each column over classified objects only, with $T_{\rm eff}$ a proxy for spectral class. ``Ratio'' is the sample column fraction over the census column fraction: 1 means the sample tracks the reference population, $>1$ over-representation}{table.10}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Amplitude completeness at the trigger, by window class and carrier morphology, from the 1200{} injections of this appendix. ``Detection'' is amplitude recovery at the nominal trigger; ``drift'' is whether a recovered drift rate is informative about the transmitter; $N$ counts the searched windows of that class. The second experiment, Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:dwell}, is \emph  {not} a threshold completeness: it injects non-drifting carriers at $\geq 4\sigma $ per integration into 12{} real windows and measures temporal occupancy. The two must not be read across.}}{24}{table.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:classcomp}{{11}{24}{Amplitude completeness at the trigger, by window class and carrier morphology, from the \NTrials {} injections of this appendix. ``Detection'' is amplitude recovery at the nominal trigger; ``drift'' is whether a recovered drift rate is informative about the transmitter; $N$ counts the searched windows of that class. The second experiment, Table~\ref {tab:dwell}, is \emph {not} a threshold completeness: it injects non-drifting carriers at $\geq 4\sigma $ per integration into \NDwellWin {} real windows and measures temporal occupancy. The two must not be read across}{table.11}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Measured injection recovery on real ALMA data, fine-channel configuration. Recovery $C(A, f_{\rm  drift})$ rises with amplitude for drifting carriers; static and near-static ones fail the frozen criterion, and boundary-straddling tones can fail its peak-drift clause while still being detected. Coarse configurations are not plotted: under the same criterion they recover nothing, withdrawn in the text as an artefact of the criterion, not a property of the pipeline.}}{25}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:completeness}{{7}{25}{Measured injection recovery on real ALMA data, fine-channel configuration. Recovery $C(A, f_{\rm drift})$ rises with amplitude for drifting carriers; static and near-static ones fail the frozen criterion, and boundary-straddling tones can fail its peak-drift clause while still being detected. Coarse configurations are not plotted: under the same criterion they recover nothing, withdrawn in the text as an artefact of the criterion, not a property of the pipeline}{figure.7}{}}
